    "suggested_action": "replace_ja_expression",
    "reason": "The English lemma 'judge' (verb) has a broad meaning encompassing 'to form an opinion', 'to evaluate', 'to decide', and 'to act as a referee/umpire'. The Japanese expression '審判' (as '審判する') is primarily used for 'to referee/umpire' or 'to judge (a game/contest/divine judgment)'. It is too narrow to cover the general senses of the English verb 'judge'. For a general learner, '判断する' would be a more natural and appropriate translation for the core concept of 'to judge' or 'to make a judgment'.",
